Description: Patient-level survival outcomes for a whole clinical trial
  are frequently available alongside published subgroup hazard ratios,
  while the subgroup membership of each patient is not. 'retrogroup'
  reconstructs subgroup membership from these two sources of information.
  A Bayesian survival model estimates the posterior probability that each
  patient belongs to each subgroup level, and a sampling method uses these
  probabilities to impute a subgroup level for each patient.
